ove it, with zeros below each pivot.\n\nThe corresponding triangular system is\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-z&=-2 \\\\ y+2z&=-3 \\\\ z&=4\\end{aligned}\\right..\n$$\n\nBack substitution gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z&=4 \\\\ y&=-3-(2)(4)=-11 \\\\ x&=-2-(2)(-11)-(-1)(4)=24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $\\langle 24,-11,4\\rangle$." 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760764 1080 "\\langle 0,2,1\\rangle" 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760764 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760764 1083 #uuid "e0c0c019-a0fa-55e0-b49b-7e44852e3ddb" 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760765 1068 #edb/ref 17592186760741 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760765 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760765 1071 "Consider the augmented matrix\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760765 1072 #uuid "e6e99a08-cdaf-5e6f-82dd-2a007e322fb1" 13194139547563 17592186576411 true] [17592186760765 1074 "The augmented matrix is\n\n$$\nM=\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}-2 & -2 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_1:=-\\frac{1}{2}R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 3 & 4 & -7 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_2:=R_2-2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -5 & 9\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3+2R_1$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 3\\end{array}\\right].\n$$\n\nUsing $R_3:=R_3-R_2$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\left[\\begin{array}{ccc|c}1 & 1 & 